+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the providers so the model knows what to send; until now nothing checked that what came back matched it. `ToolRegistry` left that check to each tool's own executor, so every consumer implemented it differently or not at all, and a malformed call could become a confidently formatted answer built on a defaulted value. The registry now owns the check, and a malformed call becomes a tool result the model can read and correct within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## The registry validates before the executor runs
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs; a call the schema rejects returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required property and never invokes the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
+- A rejection message names the failing property path and the constraint that failed ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed value naming the path and expected type but not the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31)).
+- No rejection message and no log line ever carries an input property's value; tool input is where identifying data enters the engine, and the engine redacts nothing downstream ([validated by: keeps input values out of the rejection text and the log stream](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L136)).
+
+## What validation enforces
+
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared property types and `enum` ([validated by: rejects a value outside a declared enum without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+- Validation adds nothing: `additionalProperties` is not injected, no type is coerced, no default is applied, and there is no opt-out flag, so input the schema accepts reaches the executor unchanged, undeclared extra properties included, exactly once per call ([validated by: hands valid input to the executor unchanged, extra properties included, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- `register` compiles a static definition's schema at registration time, so an uncompilable schema throws from `register` with a message naming the tool, at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at registration time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once, and its compiled validator is reused across calls ([validated by: compiles a static schema once at registration and reuses it across calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L109)).
+- A schema produced by a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved per call, so validation uses the schema current at that call rather than a stale cached one; compiled validators are cached by the resolved schema object ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema it returns for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
+
+## Rejections flow back to the model
+
+- A schema rejection is a returned tool result, not a thrown error: `processMessage` resolves, the rejection text is visible to the provider on the next round, and a corrected retry executes normally ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back to the model and completes on the corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- The tool-round bound is what stops a rejection-and-retry cycle from spinning, since the loop asks for at most `maxToolRounds` rounds of tool calls ([validated by: stops asking for tools once maxToolRounds is spent](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L422)).
+- A tool name nothing registered still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`, unchanged: the same failure class handled the opposite way, deliberately, because direct callers already depend on the throw ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
+
+## Deliberately out of scope
+
+- Validating tool output, hallucination detection, and an evaluation harness.
+- Per-tool authorization: a schema-valid call for someone else's data is still valid, and authorization is a `ToolContext` boundary concern that no issue in this epic owns.
+- Retry, timeout and rate limiting around tool execution, and any actual tool implementation, which is written against this contract later.
